# Backend layering & secrets

## Layer contracts

| Layer | May | Must not |
|-------|-----|----------|
| `routers/` | Deps, status codes, call services, return schemas | Business rules, raw SQL, Redis OTP logic |
| `services/` | Domain rules, orchestration, email/Redis via adapters | Know FastAPI `Request`/`Response` details |
| `repositories/` | Queries, persistence | Auth decisions, HTTP |
| `schemas/` | Pydantic I/O + Field descriptions | Side effects |
| `models/` | SQLAlchemy ORM | Business workflows |

Phase features mount through `include_phase23_routers` / `include_phase456_routers`. Prefer existing service patterns (`*_service.py`, `SpineBridge` for idea status).

## Secrets

- Real SMTP / JWT / DB passwords live only in `backend/.env` (gitignored)
- Commit placeholders in `backend/.env.example` only
- Never print OTP or SMTP passwords into docs, commits, or seed files beyond the documented demo password in README

## Migrations & seed

- Schema changes → new Alembic revision under `backend/alembic/versions/`
- Demo data → `app.seed.*` modules; run after `alembic upgrade head`
